Record Types and SchemaRecord {#chapter-record-types}
=======================================

## Record Type Definition ## {#section-record-types-definition}

Every [=Record=] MUST be assigned to a Record type. A Record type:

- defines the schema of the [=payload=]
- defines the permitted states and their transitions
- defines the format requirements per state
- defines mandatory and optional [=metadata=] fields beyond `metadata.core` (see [Metadata](#chapter-metadata))
- is itself a [=Record=] of the type `SchemaRecord`


## Core Record Types ## {#section-record-types-core}

RWP defines the following core Record types (with DID Suffix):

**Relation Records:**
- `CaseRecord` (see [CaseRecord Specification](#chapter-caserecord))
- `AssertionRecord` (see [AssertionRecord  Specification](#chapter-assertionrecord))

**System Records:**
- `SchemaRecord` (see [SchemaRecord](#chapter-schema-record))
- `ConformanceRecord` (see [Conformance and Implementation Claims](#chapter-conformance))
- `DeletionRecord` (see [Payload Deletion](#chapter-deletion))
- `MergeRecord` (TBD)
- `MigrationRecord` (TBD)

The conformance requirements for these Record types are profile-, role-, and capability-specific. An implementation MUST support a core Record type only where this specification requires that support for a claimed profile, role, or exercised capability.

The capability-bound requirements are defined in [Capability-bound requirements](#section-conformance-requirements).

Additional Record types MAY be defined by organisations or standards bodies. They MUST be published as [=SchemaRecords=] and be resolvable via a DID.


## SchemaRecord ## {#chapter-schema-record}

A <dfn>SchemaRecord</dfn> is a specialised Record type that carries the definition of another Record type.

A [=SchemaRecord=] MUST:

- fulfil all requirements for a regular [=Record=] (DID, metadata, version graph)
- contain a JSON Schema (Draft 2020-12 or later, [[JSON-SCHEMA]]) in the payload
- contain the field `rwpSchemaVersion` in the payload with the RWP version for which it is valid
- contain the field `allowedStates` in the payload with the permitted states and their transitions
- contain the field `payloadFormats` in the payload with the permitted formats per state

A [=SchemaRecord=] MAY:

- contain the field `capabilities` in the payload, an array of operation identifiers (strings) declaring the functions applicable to [=Records=] of this type


**Minimal SchemaRecord payload example:**

```json
{
  "rwpSchemaVersion": "0.1",
  "schemaId": "did:rwp:bern.ch:schema-building-permit-application",
  "displayName": "Building Permit Application",
  "allowedStates": ["draft", "finalized"],
  "stateTransitions": [
    { "from": "draft", "to": "finalized", "requiresOwnerSignature": true }
  ],
  "payloadFormats": {
    "draft": ["application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document",
              "text/markdown"],
    "finalized": ["application/pdf;profile=PDF-A-2b"]
  },
  "capabilities": ["retrieve", "compare", "validate", "publish"],
  "jsonSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "type": "object",
    "required": ["parcelNumber", "applicant", "constructionProject", "date"],
    "properties": {
      "parcelNumber": { "type": "string" },
      "applicant": { "type": "string" },
      "constructionProject": { "type": "string" },
      "date": { "type": "string", "format": "date" }
    }
  }
}
```


## Schema Versioning and Backward Compatibility ## {#section-schema-record-versioning}

When a [=SchemaRecord=] is finalised in a new version, the following applies:

- Existing versions referencing an earlier schema version REMAIN valid
- The new schema MUST contain the field `previousSchemaVersion` in the payload with the hash of the predecessor schema
- Systems MUST keep all schema versions referenced by existing [=Records=] permanently accessible
- A system MUST NOT retroactively change an existing [=SchemaRecord=], corrections are made as a new version


## Capability Declaration ## {#section-schema-record-capabilities}

The `capabilities` field declares which functions are applicable to [=Records=] of the type defined by this [=SchemaRecord=]. Each entry is an operation identifier, for example `retrieve`, `compare`, `validate`, `publish`, or a Record-Type-specific operation.

The declaration is descriptive. It states that the Record Type supports an operation; it does not oblige a resolver to implement it, and it does not grant access (see [Access Control](#chapter-access-control)).

A resolver MAY use the `capabilities` of the [=SchemaRecord=] to populate the `RWP-FunctionRegistry` service entry in the DID documents of [=Records=] of this type (see [Service Entries](#subsection-did-document-service)).

A change to `capabilities` is a change to the [=SchemaRecord=] and MUST be made as a new version (see [Schema Versioning](#section-schema-record-versioning)).


